      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The prognosis of spontaneous coronary artery dissection is uncertain and optimal treatment is unknown. We previously described the first reported implantation of drug-eluting stents in spontaneous coronary artery dissection. The immediate angiographic result was good, and we now report the late clinical, angiographic and intravascular ultrasound follow up."},
